A wait leaves its thread's requests due within the span they had, whatever span it gives.
A driver that says at its wait how soon its interrupt must be answered would be answered as late as its binding says.

Caught-by: fuzz fuzz-pmp8 fuzz-rp2350 fuzz-smp2 fuzz-work test qemu-replay
Report: a wait left its caller's requests due within another span than it gave
Witness: fuzz request-wait-span

diff --git a/kernel/syscall.c b/kernel/syscall.c
--- a/kernel/syscall.c
+++ b/kernel/syscall.c
@@ -665,7 +665,6 @@ static int op_notification(struct thread *t, uint32_t slot, const struct cap *ca
             if (!span_valid(arg[1])) {
                 return KERR_INVALID_ARG;
             }
-            sched_span(t, arg[1]);
         }
         if (ntfn->bits != 0) {
             arg[1] = ntfn->bits;
